### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### PART 1 — HAPPY PATH
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Step 0 — Ping all backends through the gateway (public, no auth)
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/tokens/ping
# -> 200 token-service is running

###
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/ledger/ping
# -> 200 ledger-service is running

###
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/sync/ping
# -> 200 sync-service is running

###
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/fraud/ping
# -> 200 fraud-service is running


### Step 1 — Create a test account (ledger, internal)
POST {{base_ledger}}/api/v1/ledger/accounts/create-test-account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "initialBalance": 1000.00
}
# -> 201  {userId, totalBalance: 1000.00, availableBalance: 1000.00}


### Step 2 — Issue an offline token (token-service, internal)
###   Also reserves ₹500 via ledger: availableBalance 1000 -> 500.
###   Copy the `token` value from the response into {{offlineToken}}.
###   (The `reservationId` is NOT returned here; it is only embedded inside the
###   JWT's payload. No request in this file needs it, so leave it alone.)
POST {{base_token}}/api/v1/tokens/gettoken
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "amount": 500.00,
  "expiryHours": 6
}
# -> 201  TokenResponse {tokenId, token: <JWT>, userId, maxAmount: 500.00,
#        issuedAt, expiresAt, status: "ACTIVE", message}


### Step 3 — Check balance via gateway (proves RS256 auth + X-User-Id header)
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/ledger/balance/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionToken}}
# -> 200  {userId, totalBalance: 1000.00, availableBalance: 500.00, reservedAmount: 500.00}


### Step 4 — Validate the offline token (token-service, internal)
###   GET with a request body (call via curl/Postman if your client rejects it).
GET {{base_token}}/api/v1/tokens/validateToken
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{offlineToken}}",
  "spentAmount": 0
}
# -> 200  {valid: true, userId, reservationId, maxAmount: 500.00,
#        spentAmount: 0, reason: null}


### Step 5 — Fraud check (fraud-service, internal)
POST {{base_fraud}}/api/v1/fraud/check
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "deviceTransactionId": "txn-1",
  "offlineToken": "{{offlineToken}}",
  "deviceId": "device_1",
  "amount": 150.00,
  "merchantId": "merchant_abc",
  "transactedAt": "2026-07-31T10:30:00",
  "tokenExpiryTime": "2026-07-31T16:00:00"
}
# -> 200  {score: <small>, decision: "APPROVE", reason: "NONE"}
#        (approved iff score < 0.7)


### Step 6 — Mark used -> settles the reservation (token-service, internal)
###   ₹300 debited from total, ₹200 released back to available.
POST {{base_token}}/api/v1/tokens/mark-used
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{offlineToken}}",
  "finalSpentAmount": 300.00
}
# -> 200  "Token marked as used successfully"
#   Logs: "Token marked as USED..." then "Ledger settlement completed..."


### Step 7 — Balance after settlement (gateway)
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/ledger/balance/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionToken}}
# -> 200  {totalBalance: 700.00, availableBalance: 700.00, reservedAmount: 0.00}


### Step 8 — Token history (gateway; note token is null, status USED)
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/tokens/history/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionToken}}
# -> 200  [{tokenId, token: null, userId, maxAmount: 500.00, status: "USED", ...}]


### Step 9 — Sync a batch (gateway -> sync-service -> Kafka -> batch -> settle)
POST {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/sync/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactions": [
    {
      "deviceTransactionId": "txn-1",
      "offlineToken": "{{offlineToken}}",
      "amount": 300.00,
      "merchantId": "merchant_abc",
      "transactedAt": "2026-07-31T10:30:00"
    }
  ]
}
# -> 202  {message, acceptedCount: 1, acceptedDeviceTransactionIds: ["txn-1"]}
#   Watch sync-service logs: publish -> consume -> Spring Batch settle.


### Step 10 — Sync status for the user (gateway)
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/sync/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionToken}}
# -> 200  [OfflineTransaction with transaction status]


### Step 11 — Fraud alert list + review (gateway)
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/fraud/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionToken}}
# -> 200  [FraudAlertResponse list]

PUT {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/fraud/alerts/<ALERT_ID>/review
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "RESOLVED",
  "reviewerNotes": "false positive - trusted merchant"
}
# -> 200


### Step 12 — Gateway health passthrough (public)
GET {{base_gateway}}/actuator/sync-service/health
# -> 200  {"status":"UP"}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### PART 2 — NEGATIVE PATHS
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### N1 — Gateway: no Authorization header
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/ledger/balance/{{userId}}
# -> 401  {"error":"UNAUTHORIZED","message":"Missing or invalid Authorization header"}


### N2 — Gateway: garbage/invalid JWT
GET {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/ledger/balance/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.jwt
# -> 401  {"error":"UNAUTHORIZED","message":"Invalid or expired token"}


### N3 — Double token issue while a token is ACTIVE
POST {{base_token}}/api/v1/tokens/gettoken
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "amount": 500.00,
  "expiryHours": 6
}
# -> 400  {"errorCode":"ACTIVE_TOKEN_EXISTS","message":"User ... already has an active offline token...","timestamp":...}


### N4 — Amount out of range
POST {{base_token}}/api/v1/tokens/gettoken
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "some_other_user",
  "amount": 20000.00,
  "expiryHours": 6
}
# -> 400  {"errorCode":"VALIDATION_FAILED","message":"Request validation failed","fieldErrors":{"amount":"..."}}


### N5 — Overspend on validate
GET {{base_token}}/api/v1/tokens/validateToken
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{offlineToken}}",
  "spentAmount": 600.00
}
# -> 200  {valid: false, reason: "AMOUNT_EXCEEDS_LIMIT"}


### N6 — Replay mark-used (token is already USED)
POST {{base_token}}/api/v1/tokens/mark-used
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{offlineToken}}",
  "finalSpentAmount": 300.00
}
# -> 400  {"errorCode":"TOKEN_ALREADY_USED",...}


### N7 — Internal-only endpoint NOT routed through the gateway
POST {{base_gateway}}/api/v1/fraud/check
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}"
}
# -> 404  (no gateway route exists; services call each other directly)
